Id: sudo006e
Severity: ERROR
Category: accounts
Check: check_sudo

sudo is installed, but its rules could not be read, so what they allow
is unknown. They are read through cvtsudoers, which comes with sudo
1.8.23 and later and follows the includes and aliases; it needs root to
read /etc/sudoers. The detail gives its error. Run Tigris as root, or
on an older sudo read the rules with 'sudo -l -U USER'.
